## Signature

- Provided by: **Claude Opus 5 (anthropic/claude-opus-5)** — 2026-10-08
- Method: fresh public internet research only. Research steps attempted and their outcomes: targeted searches for `"Gemini 3.1 Flash"` with and without exclusion of the `-lite`, `TTS` and `Live` variants (returned only the suffixed models); direct fetches of `deepmind.google/models/model-cards/gemini-3-1-flash/`, `docs.cloud.google.com/.../gemini/3-1-flash`, `openrouter.ai/google/gemini-3.1-flash` and `artificialanalysis.ai/models/gemini-3-1-flash` (**all four 404**, while their `-lite` / `3-1-pro` counterparts resolve); inspection of the OpenCode Zen endpoint and pricing tables (**no such ID**); and inspection of BenchLM's model directory, which carries Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite, Flash Live Preview, Flash TTS Preview and 3.1 Pro but **no base Gemini 3.1 Flash**. `ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models` returned a transport error and could not be consulted. The repo's own `meta.json` was read only to identify what was being claimed; its OpenCode Zen free-tier claim is reported as contradicted by Zen's published docs. Benchmark data belonging to Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite was deliberately **not** imported, since that model has its own folder in this dataset. Gemini 3.1 Flash **Live** is parked as a `models_voice/` discovery per `RULES.md` and was neither created nor researched. No peer `model/` findings files were read. Unavailable items — every benchmark figure, the release date, the context window, the modalities, the pricing, the architecture, and the model's existence — are recorded as "no verified public data found" rather than estimated.
- Future sources: add a new file next to this one, e.g. `GPT_5.md`, using the same headings.
